        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 90-year-old male patient, admitted on 09/02/2018 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, clinical examination revealed reduced air entry bilaterally with audible wheeze, and oxygen saturation was below acceptable levels on room air. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed type 1 respiratory failure. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids for hydration. He responded well to treatment with improvement in symptoms and oxygen saturation. He is discharged home with a short course of oral prednisolone and optimised inhaler therapy. Please arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Yours sincerely.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
